# The build backend is a third install path no lock reached. `tox`
# installs `[build-system] requires` into its packaging env before
# either of the two a lock governs, and refuses `deps` there -- so the
# way in is `constraints` on `[pkgenv]`, which takes a requirements
# file, and this is the source it is compiled from.
#
# A mirror of `[build-system] requires` in `pyproject.toml` rather than
# a compile of it: `uv pip compile pyproject.toml` reads `[project]
# dependencies` and there is no option asking for the other table. The
# two are gated against each other by `tests/build_backend_lock_test.py`
# so the copy cannot drift.
setuptools >= 77
setuptools-scm >= 8
